.TH "PAIRDESK-UNINSTALL" "8" "November 2026" "PairDesk 2.9.3" "System Administration"
.hy
.SH NAME
.PP
pairdesk-uninstall - remove PairDesk and only the add-ons it installed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\f[B]pairdesk-uninstall\f[R] [\f[B]\[en]dry-run\f[R]]
[\f[B]\[en]yes\f[R]] [\f[B]\[en]keep-ssh-server\f[R]]
[\f[B]\[en]remove-settings\f[R]|\f[B]\[en]keep-settings\f[R]]
[\f[B]\[en]remove-tools\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Gives shared USB devices back, undoes setup, removes PairDesk and the
add-ons PairDesk installed, and keeps packages you installed yourself or
that other software needs.
Files in the shared folder are kept.
Run it as root, or from Settings > Uninstall PairDesk.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\[en]dry-run\f[R]
Show what would be removed, change nothing.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]yes\f[R]
Don\[cq]t ask before removing.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]keep-ssh-server\f[R]
Keep openssh-server even if PairDesk installed it.
.TP
\f[B]\[en]remove-settings\f[R], \f[B]\[en]keep-settings\f[R]
Remove or keep each user\[cq]s PairDesk settings and keys (default:
ask).
.TP
\f[B]\[en]remove-tools\f[R]
Also remove PairDesk\[cq]s helper programs (viewer, sshfs, usbip,
avahi-utils, xrdp\&...)
that apt records as installed by you, when nothing else uses them.
Without it, each is asked about.
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\f[B]pairdesk\f[R](1)
